    "caveats": [
      "Verify the actual channel cross-section with the device manufacturer — the 2 µL/min flow assumes a 400×100 µm rectangular channel; a different width/height changes the required flow.",
      "Confirm medium viscosity (assumed 1e-3 Pa·s, water-like); serum-containing medium is ~0.9–1.1e-3 Pa·s and shifts shear slightly.",
      "The 0.05 Pa target is the lower bound of the HepG2 physiological range (0.05–0.15 Pa); if the goal is a mid-range sinusoidal value, recalculate for a higher shear.",
      "Check the syringe pump's minimum stable flow rate — 2 µL/min is low and may require a low-dead-volume setup to avoid pulsation/backlash.",
      "PDMS absorbs lipophilic compounds; if dosing drugs, account for PDMS binding in the mass balance."
    ]
